    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>f(x)</m>, below.  It may be to your
advantage to simplify  first.</p>
<p><me>\displaystyle f(x) = \frac{x^4}{6^x}</me></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{4x^{4-1}\cdot 6^{x}-x^{4}\ln\mathopen{}\left(6\right)\cdot 6^{x}}{6^{2x}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>f'(x) = \frac{(4 x^{-1})(6^x) - (x^4) \ln(6) (6^x)}{6^{2x}}.</me></p>
</solution>
